  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leverating Partnership to achieve the goals of south Africa&apos;s HIV&amp;AIDS and STI National Strategic Plan 2007-2011 - South Africa (01-Oct-2013-31-Mar-2016)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Africa currently has one of the highest HIV prevalence rates in the world.  According to UNAIDS, in 2008 an estimated 5.7 million people are living with HIV of which approximately 3.2 million are women and 280,000 are children.  The current Single Stream of Funding is based on the Round 9 grants and is implemented along with two other Principal Recipients.  It aims to expand the National Response by capitalizing on Community-Based Organizations (CBOs) comparative advantage in service delivery for prevention, treatment, care and support.  The current grant implements activities related to behaviour change communication (BCC) community outreach to out-of-school youth, commercial sex workers, and men having sex with men, as well as for voluntary counselling and testing (VCT), community home-based care (CHBC), support to orphaned and vulnerable children (OVC), prevention of mother-to-child transmission (PMTCT), treatment, and strengthening capacity of CBOs and sub-recipients.</narrative>
  </description>
